--[[
	TechniqueData  (ReplicatedStorage/Shared/TechniqueData)
	HEXBOUND - data-driven technique definitions. Frames are at 60 FPS.
	Shared with clients for UI only (names, icons, cooldowns). The server reads this
	same table, so clients can't change balance.

	Kinds and the fields each uses:
	  Melee      : hitbox = { size, offset }, hit = {...}
	  Projectile : projectile = { speed, radius, range }, hit = {...}
	  Dash       : dash = { speed, duration }, optional hitbox + hit (a strike during the dash)
	  Burst      : hitbox (centered on the caster: offset 0), hit = {...}, knockback pushes outward

	The `hit` table uses the same fields as an M1 hit in CombatFrameData
	(damage, hitstun, blockstun, guardDamage, knockback?, unblockable?, unparryable?, hexGain?).
	Techniques default to hexGain = 0 so spending Hex doesn't refund itself.
]]

